„­bible_version£KJV¤book*§chapter	¨sections˜…¤book*§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd as Jesus passed by, he saw a man which was blind from his birth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkAnd his disciples asked him, saying, Master, who did sin, this man, or his parents, that he was born blind?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxJesus answered, Neither hath this man sinned, nor his parents: but that the works of God should be made manifest in him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcI must work the works of him that sent me, while it is day: the night cometh, when no man can work.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:As long as I am in the world, I am the light of the world.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†When he had thus spoken, he spat on the ground, and made clay of the spittle, and he anointed the eyes of the blind man with the clay,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand said unto him, Go, wash in the pool of Siloam, (which is by interpretation, Sent.) He went his way therefore, and washed, and came seeing.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThe neighbours therefore, and they which before had seen him that he was blind, said, Is not this he that sat and begged?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙISome said, This is he: others said, He is like him: but he said, I am he.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9Therefore said they unto him, How were thine eyes opened?¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶He answered and said, A man that is called Jesus made clay, and anointed mine eyes, and said unto me, Go to the pool of Siloam, and wash: and I went and washed, and I received sight.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ:Then said they unto him, Where is he? He said, I know not.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;They brought to the Pharisees him that aforetime was blind.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIAnd it was the sabbath day when Jesus made the clay, and opened his eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen again the Pharisees also asked him how he had received his sight. He said unto them, He put clay upon mine eyes, and I washed, and do see.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÈTherefore said some of the Pharisees, This man is not of God, because he keepeth not the sabbath day. Others said, How can a man that is a sinner do such miracles? And there was a division among them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuThey say unto the blind man again, What sayest thou of him, that he hath opened thine eyes? He said, He is a prophet.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut the Jews did not believe concerning him, that he had been blind, and received his sight, until they called the parents of him that had received his sight.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙcAnd they asked them, saying, Is this your son, who ye say was born blind? how then doth he now see?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]His parents answered them and said, We know that this is our son, and that he was born blind:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰but by what means he now seeth, we know not; or who hath opened his eyes, we know not: he is of age; ask him: he shall speak for himself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´These words spake his parents, because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had agreed already, that if any man did confess that he was Christ, he should be put out of the synagogue.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ2Therefore said his parents, He is of age; ask him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses›„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyThen again called they the man that was blind, and said unto him, Give God the praise: we know that this man is a sinner.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwHe answered and said, Whether he be a sinner or no, I know not: one thing I know, that, whereas I was blind, now I see.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKThen said they to him again, What did he to thee? how opened he thine eyes?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€He answered them, I have told you already, and ye did not hear: wherefore would ye hear it again? will ye also be his disciples?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTThen they reviled him, and said, Thou art his disciple; but we are Moses' disciples.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUWe know that God spake unto Moses: as for this fellow, we know not from whence he is.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒThe man answered and said unto them, Why herein is a marvellous thing, that ye know not from whence he is, and yet he hath opened mine eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtNow we know that God heareth not sinners: but if any man be a worshipper of God, and doeth his will, him he heareth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_Since the world began was it not heard that any man opened the eyes of one that was born blind.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ1If this man were not of God, he could do nothing.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrThey answered and said unto him, Thou wast altogether born in sins, and dost thou teach us? And they cast him out.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book*§chapter	«first_verse#ªlast_verse&¦verses”„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyJesus heard that they had cast him out; and when he had found him, he said unto him, Dost thou believe on the Son of God?¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCHe answered and said, Who is he, Lord, that I might believe on him?¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd Jesus said unto him, Thou hast both seen him, and it is he that talketh with thee.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ4And he said, Lord, I believe. And he worshipped him.¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book*§chapter	«first_verse'ªlast_verse)¦verses“„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And Jesus said, For judgment I am come into this world, that they which see not might see; and that they which see might be made blind.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfAnd some of the Pharisees which were with him heard these words, and said unto him, Are we blind also?¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtJesus said unto them, If ye were blind, ye should have no sin: but now ye say, We see; therefore your sin remaineth.¦layout ªlast_verse)